 // the target as if the draft were free.  This value is what both `--fit` and the MoE preflight charge instead.
+// The two-arm server's decode arm is a SECOND llama_context of the same model: it brings its own batch, scheduler,
+// compute buffers and graph cache, and it arrives AFTER the MoE expert-cache arena / movable-boundary slab has
+// sized itself from the free VRAM -- exactly like a draft context does.  So the arena must leave room for it, and
+// the reserve is charged ONLY when the pair will really be created (one predicate, DESIGN V2: a refused pair that
+// was charged leaves the arena smaller for a context that never exists).
+//
+// MEASURED (2026-11-23, gfx1201 3x R9700, 27B Q8_0, `-sm tensor -mg 0 -np 2 -c 4096`, one tiny request, VRAM
+// before/after the decode arm's reserve): +157 MiB on devices 0 and 1 and +235 MiB on device 2 (the axis the
+// extra layers land on).  The constant is that measurement rounded up -- it is headroom for ONE narrow (n_parallel
+// row) context, not a width-dependent number, because the decode arm's n_batch is n_parallel x (n_spec_max+1).
+static const int COMMON_ARMS_RESERVE_MIB = 256;
+
 static common_draft_reserve common_draft_reserve_derive(const common_params & params) {
     common_draft_reserve draft_reserve;
     if (!params.speculative.has_aux()) {
